title: The regional presidents
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: sp_party
view-if: barons_timer <= 0 and sanchez_leader = 1
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; barons_timer = 2

= The regional presidents

Susana Díaz in Andalusia, Emiliano García-Page in Castilla-La Mancha, Guillermo Fernández Vara in Extremadura, Javier Lambán in Aragón, Ximo Puig in Valencia, Javier Fernández in Asturias: each governs, each has their own electorate, and each has a view on what you should do in Madrid.

- @convene: Convene the regional presidents before deciding anything
- @executive: Consult the Federal Executive first
- @announce: Announce your strategy, then inform them
- @formal_role: Offer the barons a formal role in the negotiations
- @easy_discard

@convene
on-arrival: regional_leaders_dissent -= 8; sanchez_authority -= 2; federal_committee_balance += 3

The meeting runs for five hours. You leave with their grudging support and the feeling that you now need their permission.

@executive
on-arrival: institutionalists_dissent -= 5; modernisers_dissent -= 3; regional_leaders_dissent += 4; federal_executive_backing = 1

Your executive backs you. The barons note that they were not asked.

@announce
on-arrival: sanchez_authority += 5; member_morale += 3; regional_leaders_dissent += 12; federal_committee_balance -= 5

You set the line on television. In Seville, the reaction is icy.

@formal_role
on-arrival: regional_leaders_dissent -= 15; regional_leaders_strength += 4; sanchez_authority -= 6; barons_veto = 1

The barons join the negotiating structure. Nothing will be signed without them, which reassures them and limits you.

@membership
title: Ask the members
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: sp_party
view-if: (pact_cs = 1 or pact_up = 1) and membership_round < formation_round and membership_timer <= 0 and sanchez_leader = 1
on-arrival: {! Q.month_actions += 1; Q.membership_timer = 2; Q.membership_round = Q.formation_round || 1; !}

= Ask the members

An agreement has been signed. You could put it to a vote of the whole membership, something the PSOE has never done, before the Federal Committee can bury it.

- @consult: Hold the consultation
- @easy_discard

@consult
choose-if: funds >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough party funds.
on-arrival: funds -= 1; member_morale += 8; sanchez_authority += 6; sanchismo += 5; regional_leaders_dissent += 3; federal_committee_balance += 4

The members back the agreement by a wide margin. The barons cannot argue with the result; they argue instead about the question.

@federal_exec
title: The Federal Executive
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: sp_party
view-if: federal_exec_timer <= 0 and sanchez_leader = 1
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; federal_exec_timer = 4

= The Federal Executive

A vacancy in the party leadership gives you the chance to reshape it. Who gets the post?

- @loyalist: A loyalist from your own network
- @baron: Someone close to the regional presidents
- @unionist: A figure from the UGT tradition
- @young: A young moderniser
- @easy_discard

@loyalist
on-arrival: sanchismo += 6; federal_committee_balance += 3; regional_leaders_dissent += 5; institutionalists_dissent += 3

Your grip on Ferraz tightens. The barons notice who is being promoted.

@baron
on-arrival: regional_leaders_dissent -= 8; regional_leaders_strength += 2; sanchismo -= 3

A gesture of peace towards the federations. It costs you a seat at your own table.

@unionist
on-arrival: trade_unionists_dissent -= 8; trade_unionists_strength += 2; modernisers_dissent += 3

The UGT has a voice at the top again.

@young
on-arrival: modernisers_dissent -= 6; modernisers_strength += 2; institutionalists_dissent += 4

A fresh face for the cameras. The veterans mutter about inexperience.

@ugt
title: The UGT
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: sp_party
view-if: ugt_timer <= 0 and sanchez_leader = 1
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; ugt_timer = 4

= The UGT

The UGT's general secretary asks for a meeting. The union wants the PSOE to commit to repealing the 2012 labour reform and restoring collective bargaining.

- @commit: Commit to repealing the labour reform
- @partial: Promise to repeal its "most harmful aspects"
- @distance: Keep a polite distance
- @easy_discard

@commit
on-arrival: {! Q.trade_unionists_dissent -= 10; Q.progressives_dissent -= 4; Q.modernisers_dissent += 4; Q.rel_cs -= 4; Q.labour_promise = 2; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', {workers: 2, unemployed: 1}); } if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, 1.5, 0); } !}

A clear promise. Business and Ciudadanos will hold you to it, from the other side.

@partial
on-arrival: {! Q.trade_unionists_dissent -= 4; Q.labour_promise = 1; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0.5, 0); } !}

Enough to keep the union on side. Not enough to excite anybody.

@distance
on-arrival: {! Q.trade_unionists_dissent += 8; Q.modernisers_dissent -= 3; Q.rel_cs += 3; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, -1, 0); } !}

The union leaders leave unhappy. Your economic team is relieved.

@juventudes
title: Socialist Youth
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: sp_party
view-if: juventudes_timer <= 0 and sanchez_leader = 1
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; juventudes_timer = 4

= Socialist Youth

The Juventudes Socialistas want a campaign aimed at young voters, most of whom now vote for Podemos or Ciudadanos.

- @housing: Housing and youth rent support
- @jobs_young: Youth jobs and an end to unpaid internships
- @digital: A digital campaign run by the young members
- @easy_discard

@housing
choose-if: funds >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough party funds.
on-arrival: {! Q.funds -= 1; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', {students: 2.5, workers: 1}); } Q.modernisers_dissent -= 3; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0.5, 0); } !}

Young renters notice. Some, at least.

@jobs_young
choose-if: funds >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough party funds.
on-arrival: {! Q.funds -= 1; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', {students: 2, unemployed: 1.5}); } Q.trade_unionists_dissent -= 2; !}

A practical message for a generation of temporary contracts.

@digital
choose-if: funds >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough party funds.
on-arrival: {! Q.funds -= 1; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', {students: 3}); } Q.modernisers_dissent -= 5; Q.institutionalists_dissent += 2; !}

The memes are good. The veterans do not understand them.

@programme
title: The programme
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: sp_party
view-if: programme_timer <= 0 and sanchez_leader = 1
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; programme_timer = 6

= The programme

The party's programme conference must settle the PSOE's offer to the country. What is the centrepiece?

- @social: Social democracy: a stronger welfare state and fair taxes
- @federal: A federal Spain: constitutional reform for the territories
- @modern: Modernisation: education, science and the digital economy
- @fiscal: Fiscal credibility: no promise without a figure
- @public: Public ownership: a public bank and a public energy company
- @easy_discard

@social
on-arrival: {! if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', {workers: 1.5, pensioners: 1, unemployed: 1}); } Q.progressives_dissent -= 6; Q.trade_unionists_dissent -= 4; Q.modernisers_dissent += 3; Q.rel_up += 4; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, 1, 0); } !}

The left of the party is happy. The economists ask who pays.

@federal
on-arrival: {! Q.federal_proposal = 1; Q.rel_erc += 4; Q.rel_pnv += 4; Q.regional_leaders_dissent += 4; Q.institutionalists_dissent -= 2; Q.cat_dialogue += 1; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0, 0.8); } !}

The Granada Declaration becomes a programme. The barons support it in principle and fear it in practice.

@modern
on-arrival: {! if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', {professionals: 2, students: 1.5}); } Q.modernisers_dissent -= 6; Q.rel_cs += 3; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, -0.5, 0.3); } !}

The PSOE as a party of the future, at least on paper.

@fiscal
on-arrival: {! if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', {professionals: 1.5, self_employed: 1, pensioners: 0.5}); } Q.institutionalists_dissent -= 5; Q.progressives_dissent += 4; Q.rel_cs += 4; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, -1.2, 0); } !}

Brussels and the markets would approve. The members are less sure what the PSOE is for.

@agrupaciones
title: The local branches
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: sp_party
view-if: membership_timer <= 0 and sanchez_leader = 1
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; membership_timer = 3

= The local branches

The PSOE has nearly 190,000 members in thousands of local branches. You could spend a month among them.

- @tour: Tour the branches in your own car
- @reform_party: Promise more power for the members: primaries for every candidacy
- @easy_discard

@tour
choose-if: funds >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough party funds.
on-arrival: funds -= 1; sanchismo += 8; member_morale += 6; sanchez_authority += 2; regional_leaders_dissent += 3

You drive from branch to branch, sleeping in small hotels. The members who meet you do not forget it.

@reform_party
on-arrival: sanchismo += 5; member_morale += 8; regional_leaders_dissent += 8; institutionalists_dissent += 6; federal_committee_balance -= 3

The members cheer. The apparatus that runs the party sees the threat clearly.

@fundraising
title: Party finances
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: sp_party
view-if: fundraising_timer <= 0 and sanchez_leader = 1
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; fundraising_timer = 4

= Party finances

The party treasurer reports funds of [+ funds_display +]. Campaigns cost money, and the next one is never far away.

- @donors: A dinner with business donors (+3)
- @microdonations: An online appeal to members and sympathisers (+2)
- @bank_loan: A bank loan against future subsidies (+4, lower income for a year)
- @easy_discard

@donors
on-arrival: funds += 3; institutionalists_dissent -= 2; progressives_dissent += 4; member_morale -= 2

The cheques arrive. So do questions from the left of the party about who the PSOE listens to.

@microdonations
on-arrival: funds += 2; sanchismo += 3; member_morale += 3

Thousands of small donations. The members feel the party is theirs.

@bank_loan
on-arrival: funds += 4; loan_months = 12

The bank is happy to lend to a party with a guaranteed state subsidy. The interest will come out of future income.

@public
title: Public ownership: a public bank and a public energy company
subtitle: Popular with workers; liberals and the moderate middle class will run.
on-arrival: {! Q.progressives_dissent -= 8; Q.trade_unionists_dissent -= 4; Q.modernisers_dissent += 8; Q.institutionalists_dissent += 6; Q.rel_up += 6; Q.rel_cs -= 10; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.target(Q, 'psoe', 'working', 3); window.SpainGame.target(Q, 'psoe', 'unemployed', 2); window.SpainGame.position(Q, 3, 0); window.SpainGame.recalculate(Q); } !}

Bankia, rescued with public money, could stay public. The electricity companies' profits could fund lower bills. The left cheers; the IBEX-35, Ciudadanos and the business press warn of "Venezuela".

@dues
title: Party dues
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: sp_party
view-if: dues_timer <= 0 and sanchez_leader = 1
on-arrival: dues_timer = 6

= Party dues

The treasurer presents the accounts. Members pay [? if dues_level = 0 : the standard dues ?][? if dues_level > 0 : more than the standard dues ?][? if dues_level < 0 : less than the standard dues ?]. Income this month: [+ funds_income +] after running costs, which rise every year.

- @dues_raise: Raise the dues
- @dues_cut: Cut the dues
- @root: Leave them as they are

@dues_raise
choose-if: dues_level < 2
unavailable-subtitle: Dues are already at their highest.
on-arrival: {! Q.month_actions += 1; Q.dues_level += 1; Q.member_morale -= 5; Q.sanchismo -= 2; Q.trade_unionists_dissent += 3; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.transfer(Q, 'psoe', {up: 0.6, pp: 0.2, cs: 0.2}, {workers: 0.5, pensioners: 0.4, students: 0.4, unemployed: 0.4}); } !}

More money for Ferraz, and fewer members. Some of those who leave stop voting for the party too.

@dues_cut
choose-if: dues_level > -2
unavailable-subtitle: Dues are already at their lowest.
on-arrival: {! Q.month_actions += 1; Q.dues_level -= 1; Q.member_morale += 4; Q.sanchismo += 1; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', {workers: 0.3, students: 0.3, unemployed: 0.3}); } !}

Membership grows, especially among the young and the unemployed. The party's accounts get tighter.

@intl_network
title: Socialist International and Progressive Alliance
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: sp_party
view-if: intl_net_timer <= 0 and sanchez_leader = 1
on-arrival: intl_net_timer = 4

= Socialist International and Progressive Alliance

The PSOE belongs to both international families of the centre-left. Party money spent there builds friendships with sister parties and the chance to learn from them. What you learn depends on who leads them now, and not every lesson helps. Studying the same leadership again teaches less each time.

- @net_host: Host a Progressive Alliance conference in Madrid
- @net_labour: British Labour under [+ sister_labour +]
- @net_portugal: The Portuguese Socialists under [+ sister_portugal +]
- @net_denmark: The Danish Social Democrats under [+ sister_denmark +]
- @net_germany: The German SPD under [+ sister_germany +]
- @net_sweden: The Swedish Social Democrats under [+ sister_sweden +]
- @net_us: The US Democrats: [+ sister_us +]
- @root: Not now

@net_host
choose-if: funds >= 1.5
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 1.5 in party funds.
on-arrival: {! Q.month_actions += 1; Q.funds -= 1.5; Q.sanchez_authority += 2; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.intl(Q, 'eu', 4); window.SpainGame.intl(Q, 'south', 4); window.SpainGame.intl(Q, 'us', 2); window.SpainGame.intl(Q, 'maghreb', 2); } !}

Delegations from forty parties fill a Madrid conference centre. You are photographed with prime ministers and future prime ministers.

@net_labour
choose-if: funds >= 0.5
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 0.5 in party funds.
on-arrival: {! Q.month_actions += 1; Q.funds -= 0.5; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.learnFrom(Q, 'labour'); } !}
go-to: lesson

@net_portugal
choose-if: funds >= 0.5
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 0.5 in party funds.
on-arrival: {! Q.month_actions += 1; Q.funds -= 0.5; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.learnFrom(Q, 'portugal'); } !}
go-to: lesson

@net_denmark
choose-if: funds >= 0.5
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 0.5 in party funds.
on-arrival: {! Q.month_actions += 1; Q.funds -= 0.5; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.learnFrom(Q, 'denmark'); } !}
go-to: lesson

@net_germany
choose-if: funds >= 0.5
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 0.5 in party funds.
on-arrival: {! Q.month_actions += 1; Q.funds -= 0.5; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.learnFrom(Q, 'germany'); } !}
go-to: lesson

@net_sweden
choose-if: funds >= 0.5
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 0.5 in party funds.
